From 83c3943418052c07521ba332330a3f195602fec1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:36:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(terminal): refusals say nothing ran; scratch
 hint says it is shared

A refused foreground command (& / nohup / server guidance) rejects the whole
command, but the message never said so. An agent re-sent only the backgrounded
tail, dropping the heredoc that wrote suite.sh, and ran another session's stale
$TMPDIR/suite.sh from the host-shared scratch dir.

- terminal_tool_guards: every _FOREGROUND_GUIDANCE message ends with
  'Nothing in this command ran (...). Re-send all of it: ...'. Prefixes kept
  (evals forensics _FG_AMP still matches).
- prompt_builder: scratch line says the dir is shared by every session on the
  host; use task-unique names or mktemp. Prompt-surface snapshot regenerated.
- tests: TestRefusalSaysNothingRan (heredoc + inline &, nohup, server) and the
  scratch hint assertion; all red before, green after.

Self-heal defect agent-b3c23d31dc (card t_01a1cfbed4fade3a).
